<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gregorio Luperón</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1839–1897</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gregorio Luperón was a Dominican general and statesman, one of the leaders of the War of Restoration that ended Spanish rule in 1865. He then led the liberal Blue party against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenaventura-baez">Buenaventura Báez</a> and his Reds, opposing Báez's plan to annex the country to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. He headed a provisional government in 1879–1880.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gregorio-luperon.jpg" alt="Gregorio Luperón" width="320" height="346" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:General_Gregorio_Luper%C3%B3n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
